FINAL: **FAIL** — any check mismatch vetoes. Per PREFILL-GATE.md decision rule:
close the permutation lever; the PF-G8 GEMM B-load remap
(exl3_gemm_kernel_pf.cuh / exl3_gemm_inner_pf.cuh `pf_g8` path) does not
reproduce stock outputs. Two possible readings, both requiring harness-side
work BEFORE any pack permutation decision:
  (a) the PF-G8 GEMM remap itself is buggy (wrong address math) — lever fixable
      in the harness, gate must re-run after the fix; or
  (b) the remap is fine and the discrepancy is a harness/test-construction
      artifact (e.g. check-path scale/scale-e vs bench-path mismatch) — but
      the CPU-validated claim and the deterministic control make this less
      likely; note the harness was validated CPU-side (compile) only, never
      numerically validated on GPU before this window.
Either way: DO NOT fold PF-G8 into tools/quantize_experts_exl3.py; keep p2b
stock layout. Re-open only via a harness fix + a fresh GPU gate re-run
(bit-exactness is the binding criterion).
